ectively make detection difficult.", "image": null}, {"question": "Why do hackers often target systems that support satellites rather than the satellites themselves?", "options": ["Satellites are physically inaccessible", "Satellites are less technologically advanced", "The supporting systems are more vulnerable", "The supporting systems have less security"], "correct": 2, "explanation": "Hackers target supporting systems because they are often more vulnerable and easier to exploit than the satellites themselves, which are typically more secure and harder to access directly.", "image": null}, {"question": "What is the primary reason satellites are considered 'smart' and will become even smarter?", "options": ["Increased processing power", "Improved hardware capabilities", "Enhanced software functionality", "All of the above"], "correct": 3, "explanation": "Satellites are becoming smarter due to advancements in various areas including processing power, hardware, and software. The slide mentions 'More than patching software' and 'Secure-by-design' engineering, indicating a holistic approach to making satellites more intelligent and secure.", "image": null}, {"question": "Which of the following is NOT a processor-based sub-system listed in the spacecraft systems slide?", "options": ["Attitude & Orbit Control Electronics (AOCE)", "Telecommand Command Processing (TCP)", "Data Handling Systems (SSR etc.)", "Sensors (Gyro, AccMtr, ES, SS, Star Sensors)"], "correct": 3, "explanation": "Sensors are hardware components that provide measurements and do not necessarily involve processing like the other listed sub-systems.", "image": null}, {"question": "What is the primary function of the Telecommand Command Processing (TCP) system in a spacecraft?", "options": ["To process and execute commands received from ground stations", "To control the spacecraft's attitude and orbit", "To handle data storage and transmission", "To process sensor data for navigation"], "correct": 0, "expl